  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drought mitigation project for Gokwe, Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe is currently experiencing an El Ni&#xF1;o-stimulated dry spell, characterised by extremely hot and dry weather conditions, which have left people and livestock in the two districts in a desperate situation as relates to food security, water availability and livestock rearing.  As expected, households in regions 4 and 5 will be seriously affected by this dry spell, with the delayed rains causing a drastic reduction in area planted, while the crop that had already been planted has wilted. In Gokwe the rain season started mid-December (instead of end of October 2015) and it did not reach field capacity. While the actual reduction in area planted will be confirmed during the post planting survey planned for February 2016, it is already anticipated that there will be food shortages in Gokwe. 
This project seeks to propose a series of activities that could be implemented to strengthen household adaptation to the dry spell.</narrative>
  </description>
